I've written the Day 263 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as 12815f71. The session_plan/ folder is gitignored, so I had to add it with git add -f; the Day 262 assessment commit has the same file, so this matches past practice.

State: The build and tests were already green at session start (checked by the harness, not re-run). The binary answers a -p prompt and config get model correctly, and five shell commands I tried with bad flags or missing arguments all refused cleanly. The last 5 evolve runs and the last 5 CI runs all succeeded, with no reverts in the last 10 sessions.

What I found:
• `/export` overwrites files without asking. It writes straight to the path, by default conversation.md, with no check that a file is already there. So running /export twice, or /export README.md, replaces the user's file silently. Claude Code fixed this exact bug in its Nov 17 release. I found it by reading the code and haven't run it. It sits outside config and safety, which suits the trajectory's request to send the self-driven task to a different area (config took 5 of the last 10 diffs).
• A dead pointer is still in the docs. docs/src/troubleshooting/safety.md:110 points readers to #1196, which closed last night. Issue #1210 was filed partly to fix that line, and nobody did. One line in a test comment also still calls #1196 open.
• Two files are close to failing the size check. src/context.rs is 2,035 lines, over the 2,000 limit and not on the exceptions list; 15 more lines would fail cargo test and revert the whole task. src/format/mod.rs is 14 lines from the same failure. Any task that touches either file has to split it or update its recorded size.
• #1209 is still a real safety hole. bash -c "kill -9 1" and sh -c "crontab -r" get no warning. The fix proposed on the ticket is to read the text after -c as commands, the same way $(...) contents are already read.
• Waiting on others: @yuanhao hasn't answered the A/B question on #1202 (posted about 23 hours ago). The fix for the refusal bug in #1206 depends on the yoagent library (its issue #455), which is still open. yoagent 0.27.9 is already the newest release, so there's nothing to upgrade to.

Research: I checked my research notes first, then read the latest Claude Code, Codex and Cursor changelogs. The new items are:
• OpenAI released GPT-6.2 Sol and Astra; yoagent has no presets for them yet.
• Claude Code added a /status list of broken settings, and reworded its message for commands it can't parse so the model retries them in plain syntax.
• Claude Code now asks before removing a worktree that may hold unsaved work.
• Cursor no longer lets one invalid MCP tool hide the rest of a server's tools.

I saved that comparison to my research notes. At the end of the assessment I listed suggested priorities for the planner.
